{"abstract":"A choreography gives a description of how endpoints in a concurrent systems should exchange messages during its execution. In this paper, we informally introduce a choreographic language for describing security protocols and a property language for expressing non-trivial security properties of such protocols. We motivate this work using the envelope protocol [2] as an example, which ensures auditable transfers by means of a TPM, that guarantees that the issuer of a message always learns whether such message has been opened or not. We then take an implementation of the TPM formulated as an API and discuss how such implementation and the usage of the TPM in the protocol can be related. Finally, we illustrate how the protocol and property descriptions can be translated into multiset rewrite rules and metric first order logic respectively, in order to check if auditable transfer holds.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Bruni, Alessandro","Carbone, Marco","Giustolisi, Rosario","Mödersheim, Sebastian Alexander","Schürmann, Carsten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-310372"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Choreography","Security protocols","Verification"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"security protocols as choreographies","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/265046987/Bruni2021_Chapter_SecurityProtocolsAsChoreograph.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-310372","identifier":[{"id":"85119665514","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-13355403-b681-442d-9e5e-d2239d8a164e"],"keyword":["Choreography","Security protocols","Verification"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0EA9D1A4E0EF8BC005FCFD2FF0A70B10"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/265046987/Bruni2021_Chapter_SecurityProtocolsAsChoreograph.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Formal Methods"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alessandro","key":"brunipau","last":"Bruni","name":"Bruni, Alessandro","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marco","key":"carbonepau","last":"Carbone","name":"Carbone, Marco","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rosario","key":"giustolisipau","last":"Giustolisi","name":"Giustolisi, Rosario","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sebastian Alexander","key":"mödersheimpau","last":"Mödersheim","locid":"21eb3855-68a7-4647-a3a0-8526af03169f","name":"Mödersheim, Sebastian Alexander","orcid":"0000-0002-6901-8319","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten","key":"schürmannpau","last":"Schürmann","name":"Schürmann, Carsten","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Daniel","key":"doughertypedh","last":"Dougherty","name":"Dougherty, Daniel","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"José","key":"meseguerpedh","last":"Meseguer","name":"Meseguer, José","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Sebastian Alexander","key":"mödersheimpedh","last":"Mödersheim","name":"Mödersheim, Sebastian Alexander","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Paul","key":"rowepedh","last":"Rowe","name":"Rowe, Paul","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-030-91631-2_5","isbn":["9783030916305"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"98-111","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"Essays Dedicated to Joshua Guttman on the Occasion of his 66.66th Birthday","title":"Protocols, Strands, and Logic"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85119665514"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-13355403-b681-442d-9e5e-d2239d8a164e"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Security Protocols as Choreographies","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-310372","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"The operation of trimming data sets is heavily used in AI systems. Trimming is useful to make AI systems more robust against adversarial or common perturbations. At the core of robust AI systems lies the concept that outliers in a data set occur with low probability, and therefore can be discarded with little loss of precision in the result. The statistical argument that formalizes this concept of robustness is based on an extension of the Chebyshev’s inequality first proposed by Tukey in 1960. In this paper we present a mechanized proof of robustness of the trimmed mean algorithm, which is a statistical method underlying many complex applications of deep learning. For this purpose we use the Coq proof assistant to formalize Tukey’s extension to Chebyshev’s inequality, which allows us to verify the robustness of the trimmed mean algorithm. Our contribution shows the viability of mechanized robustness arguments for algorithms that are at the foundation of complex AI systems.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Daukantas, Ieva","Bruni, Alessandro","Schürmann, Carsten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-730162"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Formal verification","Machine learning","Proof","Robustness","robust mean estimation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"trimming data sets a verified algorithm for robust mean estimation","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/103430600/3479394.3479412.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-730162","ids":["itu-2340c322-f124-413f-81e7-df35c0678052"],"keyword":["Formal verification","Machine learning","Proof","robust mean estimation","robustness"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-32B38958CF77E0C89893BED43971820E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/103430600/3479394.3479412.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ieva","key":"daukantaspau","last":"Daukantas","locid":"2d051ceb-fa4a-4a33-b059-ed443d8c79cc","name":"Daukantas, Ieva","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alessandro","key":"brunipau","last":"Bruni","locid":"5c50bbc9-ed3d-417f-ba4d-e484eaf536b3","name":"Bruni, Alessandro","orcid":"0000-0003-2946-9462","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten","key":"schürmannpau","last":"Schürmann","locid":"1313519f-2074-41d6-8b79-589648e37211","name":"Schürmann, Carsten","orcid":"0000-0003-4793-0099","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of PPDP (Principles of Declarative Programing Languages)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-2340c322-f124-413f-81e7-df35c0678052"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Trimming Data Sets: a Verified Algorithm for Robust Mean Estimation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-730162","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"author_count":5,"contributors":["Ryan, Peter","Jamroga, Wojtek","Schneider, Steve","Schürmann, Carsten","Stark, Philip"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382373"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Luxembourg","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Universite du Luxembourg","University of California","University of Surrey"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a declaration of software independence","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-382373","ids":["itu-4a10ab2f-c232-4a71-996c-be66905d5bdb"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-63698B21D45DC5820DA31F447B08A163"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"lu","key":"universite du luxembourg","loc":["Luxembourg","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Universite du Luxembourg","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of surrey","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Surrey","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Information Security and Trust","IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"university of california","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of California","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"ryanpau","last":"Ryan","name":"Ryan, Peter","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Wojtek","key":"jamrogapau","last":"Jamroga","name":"Jamroga, Wojtek","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Steve","key":"schneiderpau","last":"Schneider","name":"Schneider, Steve","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten","key":"schürmannpau","last":"Schürmann","locid":"1313519f-2074-41d6-8b79-589648e37211","name":"Schürmann, Carsten","orcid":"0000-0003-4793-0099","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Philip","key":"starkpau","last":"Stark","name":"Stark, Philip","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Festschrift for Joshua Guttman"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-4a10ab2f-c232-4a71-996c-be66905d5bdb"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A Declaration of Software Independence","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382373","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Risk-limiting audits (RLAs) are expected to strengthen the public confidence in the correctness of an election outcome. We hypothesize that this is not always the case, in part because for large margins between the winner and the runner-up, the number of ballots to be drawn can be so small that voters lose confidence. We conduct a user study with 105 participants resident in the US. Our findings confirm the hypothesis, showing that our study participants felt less confident when they were told the number of ballots audited for RLAs.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Dalela, Asmita","Kulyk, Oksana","Schürmann, Carsten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383795"],"event":{"acronym":"E-VOTE-ID","title":"International Joint Conference on Electronic Voting"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Election confidence","Risk limiting audits","User study","ballot auditing","election margins"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"voter perceptions of trust in risk limiting audit","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86390718/Trust_in_RLAs_E_Vote_ID_12.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-383795","ids":["itu-ae2d33dc-5750-4af2-b875-03151ea74fae"],"keyword":["ballot auditing","election confidence","election margins","risk-limiting audits","user study"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-C452B134F997BAABE1E7E25AFE271389"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86390718/Trust_in_RLAs_E_Vote_ID_12.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Asmita","key":"dalelapau","last":"Dalela","name":"Dalela, Asmita","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Oksana","key":"kulykpau","last":"Kulyk","locid":"1dbd1112-eb47-4406-936c-6807e8845610","name":"Kulyk, Oksana","orcid":"0000-0003-4218-1658","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten","key":"schürmannpau","last":"Schürmann","locid":"1313519f-2074-41d6-8b79-589648e37211","name":"Schürmann, Carsten","orcid":"0000-0003-4793-0099","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"publisher":"TalTech press","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the Sixth International Joint Conference on Electronic Voting (E-Vote-ID 2021)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-ae2d33dc-5750-4af2-b875-03151ea74fae"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Voter Perceptions of Trust in Risk-Limiting Audit","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383795","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"A choreography gives a description of how endpoints in a concurrent systems should exchange messages during its execution. In this paper, we informally introduce a choreographic language for describing security protocols and a property language for expressing non-trivial security properties of such protocols. We motivate this work using the envelope protocol [2] as an example, which ensures auditable transfers by means of a TPM, that guarantees that the issuer of a message always learns whether such message has been opened or not. We then take an implementation of the TPM formulated as an API and discuss how such implementation and the usage of the TPM in the protocol can be related. Finally, we illustrate how the protocol and property descriptions can be translated into multiset rewrite rules and metric first order logic respectively, in order to check if auditable transfer holds.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Bruni, Alessandro","Carbone, Marco","Giustolisi, Rosario","Mödersheim, Sebastian Alexander","Schürmann, Carsten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381950"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Auditable Transfers","Choreographic Language","Multiset Rewrite Rules","Security protocols","Trusted Platform Module TPM"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"security protocols as choreographies","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/portalfiles/portal/265046987/Bruni2021_Chapter_SecurityProtocolsAsChoreograph.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381950","identifier":[{"id":"85119665514","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-2e5fa3e9-40e9-4a60-9ec5-30b1f20eb36c"],"keyword":["Auditable Transfers","Choreographic Language","Multiset Rewrite Rules","Security Protocols","Trusted Platform Module (TPM)"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-FF5FA21AA3B264DC55D51E3BCD2AF690"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/portalfiles/portal/265046987/Bruni2021_Chapter_SecurityProtocolsAsChoreograph.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Information Security and Trust","IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alessandro","key":"brunipau","last":"Bruni","locid":"5c50bbc9-ed3d-417f-ba4d-e484eaf536b3","name":"Bruni, Alessandro","orcid":"0000-0003-2946-9462","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marco","key":"carbonepau","last":"Carbone","locid":"9027b41a-4159-4db7-9ddd-8fc8f41f1fb3","name":"Carbone, Marco","orcid":"0000-0001-9479-2632","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rosario","key":"giustolisipau","last":"Giustolisi","locid":"62db65c9-470c-472f-b039-6c4a704ef170","name":"Giustolisi, Rosario","orcid":"0000-0002-2917-9601","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian Alexander","key":"mödersheimpau","last":"Mödersheim","name":"Mödersheim, Sebastian Alexander","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten","key":"schürmannpau","last":"Schürmann","locid":"1313519f-2074-41d6-8b79-589648e37211","name":"Schürmann, Carsten","orcid":"0000-0003-4793-0099","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"98","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","subtitle":"Joshua Guttman's Festschrift","title":"Security Protocols as Choreographies"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-2e5fa3e9-40e9-4a60-9ec5-30b1f20eb36c"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Security Protocols as Choreographies","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381950","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Risk-limiting audits (RLAs) are expected to strengthen the public confidence in the correctness of an election outcome. We hypothesize that this is not always the case, in part because for large margins between the winner and the runner-up, the number of ballots to be drawn can be so small that voters lose confidence. We conduct a user study with 105 participants resident in the US. Our findings confirm the hypothesis, showing that our study participants felt less confident when they were told the number of ballots audited for RLAs. We elaborate on our findings and propose recommendations for future use of RLAs.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Dalela, Asmita","Kulyk, Oksana","Schürmann, Carsten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384442"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Audit methodology","Ballot sampling","Election confidence","Election integrity","Risk limiting audits","User study","Voter perception"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"voter perceptions of trust in risk limiting audits extended","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86215458/Trust_in_RLAs_E_Vote_ID_extended.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384442","ids":["itu-d7a4dda1-96db-4e14-945a-6aee4de431c7"],"keyword":["Audit methodology","Ballot sampling","Election confidence","Election integrity","Risk-limiting audits","User study","Voter perception"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-2A3B08C508818C7A31E8FF736912E97A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86215458/Trust_in_RLAs_E_Vote_ID_extended.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Asmita","key":"dalelapau","last":"Dalela","name":"Dalela, Asmita","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Oksana","key":"kulykpau","last":"Kulyk","locid":"1dbd1112-eb47-4406-936c-6807e8845610","name":"Kulyk, Oksana","orcid":"0000-0003-4218-1658","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten","key":"schürmannpau","last":"Schürmann","locid":"1313519f-2074-41d6-8b79-589648e37211","name":"Schürmann, Carsten","orcid":"0000-0003-4793-0099","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-d7a4dda1-96db-4e14-945a-6aee4de431c7"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Voter Perceptions of Trust in Risk-Limiting Audits (Extended)","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384442","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Cybersecurity awareness training has a bad reputation for being ineffective and boring [21]. In this paper, we show the contrary, namely that it is possible to deliver effective cybersecurity awareness training using e-learning. We provide a general methodology on how to create cybersecurity awareness training and evaluate it based on Kirkpatrick’s model of evaluation [22]. We have conducted a pilot study of the methodology in context of the European Parliament election 2019.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Schürmann, Carsten","Jensen, Lisa Hartmann","Sigbjörnsdóttir, Rosa"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-385007"],"event":{"acronym":"E-VOTE-ID","title":"International Joint Conference on Electronic Voting"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cybersecurity Awareness Training","E learning","European Parliament Election 2019","Kirkpatrick s Model","Methodology Evaluation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effective cybersecurity awareness training for election officials","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-030-60347-2_13","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-385007","identifier":[{"id":"85092172734","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-fed9bf83-0620-49b7-ae32-4fb45beabf59"],"keyword":["Cybersecurity Awareness Training","E-learning","European Parliament Election 2019","Kirkpatrick’s Model","Methodology Evaluation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C51B138259A5C34FBAB08D4743CB10B7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85694680/Sch_rmann2020_Chapter_EffectiveCybersecurityAwarenes.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-030-60347-2_13","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Information Security and Trust","IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten","key":"schürmannpau","last":"Schürmann","locid":"1313519f-2074-41d6-8b79-589648e37211","name":"Schürmann, Carsten","orcid":"0000-0003-4793-0099","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lisa Hartmann","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Lisa Hartmann","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Rosa","key":"sigbjörnsdóttirpau","last":"Sigbjörnsdóttir","name":"Sigbjörnsdóttir, Rosa","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-030-60347-2_13","eisbn":["9783030603472"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"196-212","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"E-Vote-ID 2020","title":"Electronic Voting"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85092172734"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-fed9bf83-0620-49b7-ae32-4fb45beabf59"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Effective Cybersecurity Awareness Training for Election Officials","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-385007","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"In this paper we analyze the security of the online Danish party endorsement system (DVE) and present two attacks: one technical, which we discovered during our study of the system in 2016 and which compromises the integrity of the endorsements stored in the DVE-database and another socio-technical, which allows parties to circumvent mechanisms to protect voters against abuse. To understand these attacks, we introduce the legal and technical frameworks of the DVE-system, analyze its problems, and describe a sequence of events that has led to endorsing three new parties that stood in the 2019 Danish Parliament election.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Schürmann, Carsten","Bruni, Alessandro"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-695279"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["DVE system","Danish election integrity","Security analysis","Socio technical attacks","Technical attacks"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"technical and socio technical attacks on the danish party endorsement system","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85076094745","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-695279","identifier":[{"id":"85076094745","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-b0634774-5bb1-4384-b95e-5a4c85038c97"],"keyword":["DVE system","Danish election integrity","Security analysis","Socio-technical attacks","Technical attacks"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7544FA7B819579A0A8369F38E5A1959E"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Information Security and Trust","IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten","key":"schürmannpau","last":"Schürmann","locid":"1313519f-2074-41d6-8b79-589648e37211","name":"Schürmann, Carsten","orcid":"0000-0003-4793-0099","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alessandro","key":"brunipau","last":"Bruni","locid":"5c50bbc9-ed3d-417f-ba4d-e484eaf536b3","name":"Bruni, Alessandro","orcid":"0000-0003-2946-9462","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9783030306250"],"pages":"200-215","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Electronic Voting","volume":"LLNCS11759"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85076094745"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-b0634774-5bb1-4384-b95e-5a4c85038c97"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Technical and Socio-Technical Attacks on the Danish Party Endorsement System","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-695279","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Body-fat distribution is a risk factor for adverse cardiovascular health consequences. We analyzed the association of body-fat distribution, assessed by waist-to-hip ratio adjusted for body mass index, with 228,985 predicted coding and splice site variants available on exome arrays in up to 344,369 individuals from five major ancestries (discovery) and 132,177 European-ancestry individuals (validation). We identified 15 common (minor allele frequency, MAF ≥5%) and nine low-frequency or rare (MAF <5%) coding novel variants. Pathway/gene set enrichment analyses identified lipid particle, adiponectin, abnormal white adipose tissue physiology and bone development and morphology as important contributors to fat distribution, while cross-trait associations highlight cardiometabolic traits. In functional follow-up analyses, specifically in Drosophila RNAi-knockdowns, we observed a significant increase in the total body triglyceride levels for two genes (DNAH10 and PLXND1). We implicate novel genes in fat distribution, stressing the importance of interrogating low-frequency and protein-coding variants.","author_count":281,"contributors":["Justice, Anne E","Karaderi, Tugce","Highland, Heather M","Young, Kristin L","Graff, Mariaelisa","Lu, Yingchang","Turcot, Valérie","Auer, Paul L","Fine, Rebecca S","Guo, Xiuqing","Schurmann, Claudia","Lempradl, Adelheid","Marouli, Eirini","Mahajan, Anubha","Winkler, Thomas W","Locke, Adam E","Medina-Gomez, Carolina","Esko, Tõnu","Vedantam, Sailaja","Giri, Ayush","Lo, Ken Sin","Alfred, Tamuno","Mudgal, Poorva","Ng, Maggie C Y","Heard-Costa, Nancy L","Feitosa, Mary F","Manning, Alisa K","Willems, Sara M","Sivapalaratnam, Suthesh","Abecasis, Goncalo","Alam, Dewan S","Allison, Matthew","Amouyel, Philippe","Arzumanyan, Zorayr","Balkau, Beverley","Bastarache, Lisa","Bergmann, Sven","Bielak, Lawrence F","Blüher, Matthias","Boehnke, Michael","Boeing, Heiner","Boerwinkle, Eric","Böger, Carsten A","Bork-Jensen, Jette","Bottinger, Erwin P