{"abstract":"The process that allows one to get rewarded for returning a container through reverse vending machines (RVM) involves people and technology. In fact, it typically sees a set of human parties (e.g. customers, cashiers) and technical parties (e.g, RVMs, databases, scanners) to collaborate in order to enable eective recycling. In this paper, we advance a formal treatment of the Danish Deposit Return System (DRS). We investigate the security of the ceremony that people are expected to perform in the context of DRS using eld observation and automated reasoning tools. We give a particular focus to the security threats due to people interacting with the technology behind DRS. The ndings of our investigation enable novel considerations of the ceremony weaknesses and make it possible to delineate potential mitigations.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Garbacz, Ivan","Giustolisi, Rosario","Møller Nielsen, Kasper","Schürmann, Carsten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382429"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Automated Reasoning Tools","Deposit Return System DRS","Human Technology Interaction","Reverse Vending Machines RVM","Security Threats"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a security analysis of the danish deposit return system","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84679400/human.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382429","ids":["itu-4dbe548b-6320-4e73-a043-ed092ede44af"],"keyword":["Automated Reasoning Tools","Deposit Return System (DRS)","Human-Technology Interaction","Reverse Vending Machines (RVM)","Security Threats"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-B97D8204CE224060F96037E63A50A7C4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84679400/human.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Information Security and Trust","IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Ivan","key":"garbaczpau","last":"Garbacz","name":"Garbacz, Ivan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rosario","key":"giustolisipau","last":"Giustolisi","locid":"62db65c9-470c-472f-b039-6c4a704ef170","name":"Giustolisi, Rosario","orcid":"0000-0002-2917-9601","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Kasper","key":"møllernielsenpau","last":"Møller Nielsen","name":"Møller Nielsen, Kasper","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten","key":"schürmannpau","last":"Schürmann","locid":"1313519f-2074-41d6-8b79-589648e37211","name":"Schürmann, Carsten","orcid":"0000-0003-4793-0099","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["03029743"],"publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 9th Workshop on Socio-Technical Aspects in Security and Trust"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-4dbe548b-6320-4e73-a043-ed092ede44af"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A Security Analysis of th