,"rank":316,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"L Adrienne","key":"cupplesladriennepau","last":"Cupples","name":"Cupples, L Adrienne","rank":317,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28443625"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/ncomms14977","issn":["20411723"],"journal":"Nature Communications","paperid":"14977","status":"p","title":"Nature Communications","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85019322396"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-52ae0d5b-8b57-4320-b771-4af04148e46e"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Genome-wide meta-analysis of 241,258 adults accounting for smoking behaviour identifies novel loci for obesity traits","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-442792","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"We present an automated data collection technique called white boxes-or simply wb-technique, which is designed to analyze the voter behavior in polling stations including the measurement of arrival and waiting times and the determination of arrival frequency, to assist the management of polling places to make decisions regarding the distribution of resources and to identify areas for future improvement, and to provide hard data to guide the political decision making process with respect to the choice of voting technologies.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Schürmann, Carsten","Wang, Jian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384206"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Automated Data Collection","Polling station management","Resource distribution optimization","Voter behavior analysis","Voting Technology Decision making"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"measuring voter lines","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85010417592","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384206","identifier":[{"id":"85010417592","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-c86c121f-79b3-4c11-9ac2-da5072741ac6"],"keyword":["Automated data collection","Polling station management","Resource distribution optimization","Voter behavior analysis","Voting technology decision-making"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8143123CF404D95BE5E32E058B562124"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten","key":"schürmannpau","last":"Schürmann","locid":"1313519f-2074-41d6-8b79-589648e37211","name":"Schürmann, Carsten","orcid":"0000-0003-4793-0099","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jian","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Jian","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/cedem.2016.16","eisbn":["9781509010431"],"isbn":["9781509010424"],"pages":"57-65","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","subtitle":"CeDEM 16","title":"Proceedings of the 6th International Conference for E-Democracy and Open Government"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85010417592"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-c86c121f-79b3-4c11-9ac2-da5072741ac6"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Measuring Voter Lines","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384206","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"This paper takes up the question of transparency in electronically enabled elections (e-voting). The principle of transparency is central to electoral governance as it provides means for electoral stakeholders to observe and ensure the integrity of an election. However, the issue of transparency in the field of e-voting has been proved to be di cult to tackle practically as well as analytically. In this paper we introduce the notion of ‘frames of transparency’ and deploy it to conduct a comparative analysis of three e-votes counting ceremonies in Norway, Estonia and Australia. We ask the question of how transparency is framed during these ceremonies, that is what features of the electronic votes counting process are made visible and what others are omitted. Our analysis reveals that e-voting ceremonies emphasizes bureaucratic and technocratic frames of transparency, while the democratic frame is the most di cult to uphold.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Schürmann, Carsten","Markussen, Randi","Bélanger, Olivier","Ronquillo, Lorena"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382338"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Comparative analysis","E voting","Electoral Governance","Frames of Transparency","Transparency"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"framing electoral transparency a comparative analysis of three e votes counting ceremonies","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82440079/Framing_Electoral_Transparency_A_Comparative_Analysis_of_Three_E_vote_Counting_Ceremonies.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382338","ids":["itu-47aff0da-f801-49f9-ab86-20afecd99687"],"keyword":["Comparative Analysis","E-voting","Electoral Governance","Frames of Transparency","Transparency"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-99D121C941DB39F62C6BC54DBCDB2B68"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82440079/Framing_Electoral_Transparency_A_Comparative_Analysis_of_Three_E_vote_Counting_Ceremonies.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten","key":"schürmannpau","last":"Schürmann","locid":"1313519f-2074-41d6-8b79-589648e37211","name":"Schürmann, Carsten","orcid":"0000-0003-4793-0099","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Randi","key":"markussenpau","last":"Markussen","name":"Markussen, Randi","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Olivier","key":"bélangerpau","last":"Bélanger","name":"Bélanger, Olivier","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Lorena","key":"ronquillopau","last":"Ronquillo","name":"Ronquillo, Lorena","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-47aff0da-f801-49f9-ab86-20afecd99687"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Framing Electoral Transparency: A comparative analysis of three e-votes counting ceremonies","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382338","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Wadler introduced Classical Processes (CP), a calculus based on a propositions-as-types correspondence between propositions of classical linear logic and session types. Carbone et al. introduced Multiparty Classical Processes, a calculus that generalises CP to multiparty session types, by replacing the duality of classical linear logic (relating two types) with a more general notion of coherence (relating an arbitrary number of types). This paper introduces variants of CP and MCP, plus a new intermediate calculus of Globally-governed Classical Processes (GCP). We show a tight relation between these three calculi, giving semantics-preserving translations from GCP to CP and from MCP to GCP. The translation from GCP to CP interprets a coherence proof as an arbiter process that mediates communications in a session, while MCP adds annotations that permit processes to communicate directly without centralised control.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Carbone, Marco","Lindley, Sam","Montesi, Fabrizio","Schürmann, Carsten","Wadler, Philip"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382521"],"event":{"acronym":"CONCUR","title":"International Conference on Concurrency Theory"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Edinburgh"],"keyword":["Calculus of Processes","Classical Processes","Coherence Proofs","Linear Logic","Multiparty Session Types"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"coherence generalises duality a logical explanation of multiparty session types","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.CONCUR.2016.33","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382521","identifier":[{"id":"85012907940","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-53c8ea8b-f006-4cba-b6cd-159c9c41d2b3"],"keyword":["Calculus of Processes","Classical Processes","Coherence Proofs","Linear Logic","Multiparty Session Types"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-3-3C311C93112302E1F106231191870530"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82354751/LIPIcs_CONCUR_2016_33.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.CONCUR.2016.33","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics","The Department, Theoretical Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of edinburgh","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Edinburgh","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["University of Southern Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marco","key":"carbonepau","last":"Carbone","locid":"9027b41a-4159-4db7-9ddd-8fc8f41f1fb3","name":"Carbone, Marco","orcid":"0000-0001-9479-2632","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Sam","key":"lindleypau","last":"Lindley","name":"Lindley, Sam","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Fabrizio","key":"montesipau","last":"Montesi","name":"Montesi, Fabrizio","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten","key":"schürmannpau","last":"Schürmann","locid":"1313519f-2074-41d6-8b79-589648e37211","name":"Schürmann, Carsten","orcid":"0000-0003-4793-0099","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Philip","key":"wadlerpau","last":"Wadler","name":"Wadler, Philip","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4230/lipics.concur.2016.33","issn":["18688969"],"journal":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics","pages":"1-15","paperid":"33","publisher":"Schloss Dagstuhl - Leibniz-Zentrum fuer Informatik GmbH","status":"p","title":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics","title_org":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics (LIPIcs)","volume":"59"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85012907940"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-53c8ea8b-f006-4cba-b6cd-159c9c41d2b3"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Coherence Generalises Duality: A Logical Explanation of Multiparty Session Types","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382521","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"In this paper we propose a logical foundation of processes and their focused normal forms. We use a linear meta-language based on substructural operational semantics to describe focused forms of processes, and compare them to standard π-calculus processes with their respective operational semantics. The overall goal of this research is to understand how to reason about processes, multiparty communication and global types, and how to mechanize properties such as deadlock freeness and liveness. We are also interested in establishing the limitations of this approach.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Bock, Peter Brottveit","Murawska, Agata","Bruni, Alessandro","Schürmann, Carsten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381460"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Deadlock freeness and liveness","Focused normal forms","Linear meta language","Logical foundations of processes","Substructural operational semantics"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"representing session types","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"doi","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/Representing-Session-Types-Bock-Bruni/3504a09d57adb7b7844e419f29ab4b2cb633c1ff","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381460","ids":["itu-0d096f4a-7074-4091-88f2-2bed4ed4a216"],"keyword":["Deadlock freeness and liveness","Focused normal forms","Linear meta-language","Logical foundations of processes","Substructural operational semantics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-14A561EA885F3DE32C112CDD67E5454D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/Representing-Session-Types-Bock-Bruni/3504a09d57adb7b7844e419f29ab4b2cb633c1ff","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82468059/bock_etal.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter Brottveit","key":"bockpau","last":"Bock","name":"Bock, Peter Brottveit","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Agata","key":"murawskapau","last":"Murawska","name":"Murawska, Agata","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alessandro","key":"brunipau","last":"Bruni","locid":"5c50bbc9-ed3d-417f-ba4d-e484eaf536b3","name":"Bruni, Alessandro","orcid":"0000-0003-2946-9462","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten","key":"schürmannpau","last":"Schürmann","locid":"1313519f-2074-41d6-8b79-589648e37211","name":"Schürmann, Carsten","orcid":"0000-0003-4793-0099","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-0d096f4a-7074-4091-88f2-2bed4ed4a216"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Representing Session Types","type":"Other-Internet Publication","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381460","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Wadler introduced Classical Processes (CP), a calculus based on a propositions-as-types correspondence between propositions of classical linear logic and session types. Carbone et al. introduced Multiparty Classical Processes, a calculus that generalises CP to multiparty session types, by replacing the duality of classical linear logic (relating two types) with a more general notion of coherence (relating an arbitrary number of types). This paper introduces variants of CP and MCP, plus a new intermediate calculus of Globally-governed Classical Processes (GCP). We show a tight relation between these three calculi, giving semantics-preserving translations from GCP to CP and from MCP to GCP. The translation from GCP to CP interprets a coherence proof as an arbiter process that mediates communications in a session, while MCP adds annotations that permit processes to communicate directly without centralised control. © Marco Carbone, Sam Lindley, Fabrizio Montesi, Carsten Schürmann, and Philip Wadler; licensed under Creative Commons License CC-BY.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Carbone, Marco","Lindley, Sam","Montesi, Fabrizio","Schürmann, Carsten","Wadler, Philip"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-594094"],"event":{"acronym":"CONCUR","end":"2016-08-26","place":"Québec City, ca","start":"2016-08-23","title":"27th International Conference on Concurrency Theory","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","The University of Edinburgh"],"keyword":["Linear Logic","Multiparty Session Types"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"coherence generalises duality a logical explanation of multiparty session types","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.CONCUR.2016.33","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-594094","identifier":[{"id":"85012907940","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-48d05001-80c1-4f13-9f6f-82b33da844fe"],"keyword":["Linear logic","Multiparty Session Types, Linear Logic, Propositions as Types","Multiparty session types","Propositions as types"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-3-3C311C93112302E1F106231191870530"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.CONCUR.2016.33","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/129416303/Coherence_generalises_duality.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"the university of edinburgh","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"The University of Edinburgh","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marco","key":"carbonepau","last":"Carbone","name":"Carbone, Marco","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Sam","key":"lindleypau","last":"Lindley","name":"Lindley, Sam","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Fabrizio","key":"montesipau","last":"Montesi","locid":"81d9220c-ba43-48b1-aa21-129c942a9c92","name":"Montesi, Fabrizio","orcid":"0000-0003-4666-901X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten","key":"schürmannpau","last":"Schürmann","name":"Schürmann, Carsten","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Philip","key":"wadlerpau","last":"Wadler","name":"Wadler, Philip","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Josée","key":"desharnaispedh","last":"Desharnais","name":"Desharnais, Josée","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Radha","key":"jagadeesanpedh","last":"Jagadeesan","name":"Jagadeesan, Radha","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4230/lipics.concur.2016.33","eisbn":["9783959770170"],"issn":["18688969"],"pages":"1-15","publisher":"Schloss Dagstuhl-Leibniz-Zentrum fuer Informatik","series":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 27th International Conference on Concurrency Theory"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85012907940"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-48d05001-80c1-4f13-9f6f-82b33da844fe"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Coherence generalises duality : A logical explanation of multiparty session types","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-594094","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"We propose a Curry-Howard correspondence between a language for programming multiparty sessions and a generalisation of Classical Linear Logic (CLL). In this framework, propositions correspond to the local behaviour of a participant in a multiparty session type, proofs to processes, and proof normalisation to executing communications. Our key contribution is generalising duality, from CLL, to a new notion of n-ary compatibility, called coherence. Building on coherence as a principle of compositionality, we generalise the cut rule of CLL to a new rule for composing many processes communicating in a multiparty session. We prove the soundness of our model by showing the admissibility of our new rule, which entails deadlock-freedom via our correspondence.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Carbone, Marco","Montesi, Fabrizio","Schürmann, Carsten","Yoshida, Nobuko"],"cuid":["S02-084.11-038319"],"event":{"acronym":"CONCUR","end":"2015-09-04","place":"Madrid, es","start":"2015-09-01","title":"26th International Conference on Concurrency Theory","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Imperial College London"],"keyword":["Classical Linear Logic","Curry Howard correspondence","Deadlock freedom","Linear Logic","Multiparty Session Types","Programming Languages","Proof Normalisation","Session types","Type systems"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"multiparty session types as coherence proofs","src":["itu","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.s