of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-6fb7e123-7910-4ff9-83a9-08680ab15d72","sdu-543c40fe-373d-4fc8-bae3-9390b8e94576"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Multiparty Session Types as Coherence Proofs","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-084.11-038319","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Information and communication technologies play a critical role in the administration and organization of modern elections. Any breakdown of an election technology, security breach or programming error can incur tremendous cost for the electoral management body (EMB)—and may undermine voters’ trust, reduce voter participation or even cause national unrest. Not all of these problems are avoidable, but in most cases, good quality control can significantly reduce the likelihood that they will occur. This book is a guide on how best to achieve quality control in election technologies, such as electronic voting or tabulation systems. The key elements of quality control are certification and evaluation. Certification refers to the confirmation proof of compliance with a given standard. Evaluation is the most labour intensive part of the quality control process during which the requirements, designs, hardware, firmware, software, networks and operational contexts are examined for faults. An election technology can only be certified by third-party reviewers who are accredited to assess compliance with a standard. An EMB should consider quality control early in the process of introducing new technologies, starting during the feasibility study, and especially if it is bound by law to provide such a certification. The evaluation reports and related documents can also be used to increase the transparency of the election, improve the dialogue between EMBs and voters, and increase the EMB’s credibility.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Schürmann, Carsten","Barrat, Jordi","Bolo, Eden","Bravo, Alejandro","Krimmer, Robert","Neumann, Stephan","Acong Parreno, Al","Volkamer, Melanie","Wolf, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384114"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Estonia","Germany","Spain"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Darmstadt University of Technology","Tallinn University","University of Catalonia/URV"],"keyword":["Certification","Election technologies","Evaluation","Quality control","Voter trust"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"certification of icts in elections","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"db","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-384114","ids":["itu-c2d3cac5-19dd-4d27-8099-36d9f10c85ae"],"keyword":["Certification","Election technologies","Evaluation","Quality control","Voter trust"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-1452644A1ED9A87D22FB9CFFCC00C29C"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics","The Department, Theoretical Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"es","key":"university of catalonia urv","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Catalonia/URV","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"ee","key":"tallinn university","loc":["Estonia","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Tallinn University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"de","key":"darmstadt university of technology","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Darmstadt University of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten","key":"schürmannpau","last":"Schürmann","locid":"1313519f-2074-41d6-8b79-589648e37211","name":"Schürmann, Carsten","orcid":"0000-0003-4793-0099","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jordi","key":"barratpau","last":"Barrat","name":"Barrat, Jordi","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Eden","key":"bolopau","last":"Bolo","name":"Bolo, Eden","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Alejandro","key":"bravopau","last":"Bravo","name":"Bravo, Alejandro","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Robert","key":"krimmerpau","last":"Krimmer","name":"Krimmer, Robert","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Stephan","key":"neumannpau","last":"Neumann","name":"Neumann, Stephan","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Al","key":"acongparrenopau","last":"Acong Parreno","name":"Acong Parreno, Al","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Melanie","key":"volkamerpau","last":"Volkamer","name":"Volkamer, Melanie","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"wolfpau","last":"Wolf","name":"Wolf, Peter","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9789176710289"],"pages":"76","place":"Stockholm","publisher":"International IDEA","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-c2d3cac5-19dd-4d27-8099-36d9f10c85ae"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Certification of ICTs in Elections","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384114","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"We present an automated data collection technique called white boxes- or simply wb-technique, that is designed —to analyze the voter behavior in polling stations, which includes the measurement of arrival and waiting times, the determination of arrival frequency and multiple arrival; —to assist the management of polling places to make decision regarding the distribution of resources, and to identify areas for future improvement; —to collect historical data to evaluate the impact of redistricting and gerrymandering on the quality of the voting experience; —and to provide hard data to guide the political decision making process with respect to the choice of voting technologies.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Schürmann, Carsten","Wang, Jian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381373"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Automated Data Collection","Polling station management","Redistricting Impact","Voter behavior analysis","Voting Technology Decision making"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"measuring voter lines","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/80597561/ITU_TR_2015_191.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381373","ids":["itu-07805819-90b9-4b2b-8253-561f44db0b7b"],"keyword":["Automated Data Collection","Polling Station Management","Redistricting Impact","Voter Behavior Analysis","Voting Technology Decision-making"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-91C9E8E50BA65F6AFC4362C43B696010"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/80597561/ITU_TR_2015_191.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics","The Department, Theoretical Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten","key":"schürmannpau","last":"Schürmann","locid":"1313519f-2074-41d6-8b79-589648e37211","name":"Schürmann, Carsten","orcid":"0000-0003-4793-0099","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jian","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Jian","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["16006100"],"issue":"TR-2015-191","pages":"26","place":"Copenhagen","publisher":"IT-Universitetet i København","repno":"IT University Technical Report Series, TR-2015-191","series":"IT University Technical Report Series","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-07805819-90b9-4b2b-8253-561f44db0b7b"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Measuring Voter Lines","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381373","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Trust in the correctness of an election outcome requires proof of the correctness of vote counting. By formalising particular voting protocols as rules, correctness of vote counting amounts to verifying that all rules have been applied correctly. A proof of the outcome of any particular election then consists of a sequence (or tree) of rule applications and provides an independently checkable certificate of the validity of the result. This reduces the need to trust, or otherwise verify, the correctness of the vote counting software once the certificate has been validated. Using a rule-based formalisation of voting protocols inside a theorem prover, we synthesise vote counting programs that are not only provably correct, but also produce independently verifiable certificates. These programs are generated from a (formal) proof that every initial set of ballots allows to decide the election winner according to a set of given rules.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Schürmann, Carsten","Pattinson, Dirk"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384046"],"event":{"acronym":"AUS-AI","title":"Australasian Joint Conference on Artificial Intelligence"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Australian National University"],"keyword":["Election trust","Independently verifiable certificates","Rule based protocols","Theorem proving","Vote counting verification"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"vote counting as mathematical proof","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84952643452","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384046