{"abstract":"In Choreographic Programming, a distributed system is programmed by giving a choreography, a global description of its interactions, instead of separately specifying the behaviour of each of its processes. Process implementations in terms of a distributed language can then be automatically projected from a choreography. We present Linear Compositional Choreographies (LCC), a proof theory for reasoning about programs that modularly combine choreographies with processes. Using LCC, we logically reconstruct a semantics and a projection procedure for programs. For the first time, we also obtain a procedure for extracting choreographies from process terms.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Carbone, Marco","Montesi, Fabrizio","Schürmann, Carsten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382053"],"event":{"acronym":"CONCUR","title":"International Conference on Concurrency Theory"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Choreographic Programming","Distributed systems","Linear Compositional Choreographies","Process Automation","Semantics Reconstruction"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"choreographies logically","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84906772581","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382053","identifier":[{"id":"84906772581","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-35a5f0b1-5ec1-4d23-a209-13884ca228e2"],"keyword":["Choreographic Programming","Distributed Systems","Linear Compositional Choreographies","Process Automation","Semantics Reconstruction"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-5CEF541C508C5461A480C409A156C5C3"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics","The Department, Theoretical Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["University of Southern Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marco","key":"carbonepau","last":"Carbone","locid":"9027b41a-4159-4db7-9ddd-8fc8f41f1fb3","name":"Carbone, Marco","orcid":"0000-0001-9479-2632","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Fabrizio","key":"montesipau","last":"Montesi","name":"Montesi, Fabrizio","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten","key":"schürmannpau","last":"Schürmann","locid":"1313519f-2074-41d6-8b79-589648e37211","name":"Schürmann, Carsten","orcid":"0000-0003-4793-0099","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["03029743","16113349"],"issn_org":["03029743"],"journal":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","pages":"47-62","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","volume":"8704"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84906772581"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of S