Nore","name":"Nore, Henrik","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"wolfpau","last":"Wolf","name":"Wolf, Peter","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9789187729683"],"pages":"54","publisher":"International IDEA","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-8d174c7c-ab0c-4804-afb6-7a869bdf9349"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Use of Open Source Technology in Elections","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383340","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"The possibility to use computers for counting ballots allows us to design new voting schemes that are arguably fairer than existing schemes designed for hand-counting. We argue that formal methods can and should be used to ensure that such schemes behave as intended and conform to the desired democratic properties. Specifically, we define two semantic criteria for single transferable vote (STV) schemes, formulated in first-order logic over the theories of arrays and integers, and show how bounded model-checking and SMT solvers can be used to check whether these criteria are met. As a case study, we then analyse an existing voting scheme for electing the board of trustees for a major international conference and discuss its deficiencies.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Schürmann, Carsten","Beckert, Bernhard","Gore, Rajeev","Bormer, Thorsten","Wang, Jian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384719"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Bounded model checking","SMT solvers","Single transferable vote","Verification","Voting schemes"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"verifying voting schemes","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84906838559","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384719","identifier":[{"id":"84906838559","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-ea045b1f-58b4-4a48-b23b-6f247988571b"],"keyword":["Bounded model checking","SMT solvers","Single transferable vote","Verification","Voting schemes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6DEBDD26C304B75A188867D8637B925B"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics","The Department, Theoretical Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten","key":"schürmannpau","last":"Schürmann","locid":"1313519f-2074-41d6-8b79-589648e37211","name":"Schürmann, Carsten","orcid":"0000-0003-4793-0099","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Bernhard","key":"beckertpau","last":"Beckert","name":"Beckert, Bernhard","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Rajeev","key":"gorepau","last":"Gore","name":"Gore, Rajeev","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Thorsten","key":"bormerpau","last":"Bormer","name":"Bormer, Thorsten","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jian","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Jian","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["1873605X","22142126"],"issn_org":["22142126"],"issue":"2","journal":"Journal of Information Security and Applications","pages":"115-129","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Journal of Information Security and Applications","volume":"19"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84906838559"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-ea045b1f-58b4-4a48-b23b-6f247988571b"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Verifying Voting Schemes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384719","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"This paper discusses the Decryption and Counting Ceremony held in conjunction with the internet voting trial on election day in the Ministry of Local Government and Regional Development of Norway in 2013. We examine the organizers' ambition of making the decryption and counting of electronic votes public in order to sustain trust in internet voting. We introduce a pragmatic approach to trust that emphasises the inseparability of truth from witnessing it. Based on this and on a description of how the event was made observable and how the complexities in the counting process were disclosed, we discuss what we term economy of truth from the perspective of the IT community involved in the ceremony. We claim that broadening the economy of truth by including more explicitly social and political perspectives in the ceremony, and in internet elections in general, and how witnessing is brought about, would make a more solid case for understanding how democracy is transformed.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Markussen, Randi","Ronquillo, Lorena","Schürmann, Carsten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384591"],"event":{"acronym":"E-VOTE-ID","title":"International Joint Conference on Electronic Voting"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Decryption Ceremony","Economy of Truth","Internet voting","Observability in Voting","Trust in Electronic Voting"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"trust in internet election observing the norwegian decryption and counting ceremony","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/EVOTE.2014.7001137","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384591","identifier":[{"id":"84922570691","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-e1a37a00-8ce3-4149-b7de-38490c8bd8d6"],"keyword":["Decryption Ceremony","Economy of Truth","Internet Voting","Observability in Voting","Trust in Electronic Voting"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-15E6FDDFA75134A0C3B87A56A0EE10FE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/EVOTE.2014.7001137","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice","The Department, Interdisciplinary Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Randi","key":"markussenpau","last":"Markussen","name":"Markussen, Randi","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lorena","key":"ronquillopau","last":"Ronquillo","name":"Ronquillo, Lorena","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten","key":"schürmannpau","last":"Schürmann","locid":"1313519f-2074-41d6-8b79-589648e37211","name":"Schürmann, Carsten","orcid":"0000-0003-4793-0099","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Robert","key":"krimmerpedh","last":"Krimmer","name":"Krimmer, Robert","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Melanie","key":"volkamerpedh","last":"Volkamer","name":"Volkamer, Melanie","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/evote.2014.7001137","eisbn":["9789949236855"],"isbn":["9789949236886"],"pages":"75-82","status":"p","title":"6th International Conference on Electronic Voting (EVOTE), TUT Press, October 2014. (jcg: 26/11/14)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84922570691"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-e1a37a00-8ce3-4149-b7de-38490c8bd8d6"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Trust in Internet Election : Observing the Norwegian Decryption and Counting Ceremony","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384591","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"In Choreographic Programming, a distributed system is programmed by giving a choreography, a global description of its interactions, instead of separately specifying the behaviour of each of its processes. Process implementations in terms of a distributed language can then be automatically projected from a choreography. We present Linear Compositional Choreographies (LCC), a proof theory for reasoning about programs that modularly combine choreographies with processes. Using LCC, we logically reconstruct a semantics and a projection procedure for programs. For the first time, we also obtain a procedure for extracting choreographies from process terms.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Carbone, Marco","Montesi, Fabrizio","Schürmann, Carsten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-639762"],"event":{"acronym":"CONCUR","end":"2014-09-05","place":"Rome, it","start":"2014-09-02","title":"International conference, CONCUR 2014","year":"2014"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"choreographies logically","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-662-44584-6_5","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-639762","identifier":[{"id":"84906772581","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-e87a3f1b-eae6-4ff3-861b-b87f60273249"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-5CEF541C508C5461A480C409A156C5C3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://dx.doi.org/10.1007/978-3-662-44584-6_5","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-662-44584-6_5","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematics and Computer Science, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marco","key":"carbonepau","last":"Carbone","name":"Carbone, Marco","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Fabrizio","key":"montesipau","last":"Montesi","locid":"81d9220c-ba43-48b1-aa21-129c942a9c92","name":"Montesi, Fabrizio","orcid":"0000-0003-4666-901X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten","key":"schürmannpau","last":"Schürmann","name":"Schürmann, Carsten","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Paolo","key":"paldanpedh","last":"Paldan","name":"Paldan, Paolo","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Daniele","key":"gordapedh","last":"Gorda","name":"Gorda, Daniele","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-662-44584-6_5","eisbn":["9783662445846"],"isbn":["9783662445839"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"47-62","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"25th International Conference, CONCUR 2014, Rome, Italy, September 2-5, 2014. Proceedings","title":"CONCUR 2014 – Concurrency Theory"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84906772581"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-e87a3f1b-eae6-4ff3-861b-b87f60273249"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Choreographies, Logically","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-639762","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"We present a method for using first-order logic to specify the semantics of preferences as used in common vote counting algorithms. We also present a corresponding system that uses Celf linear-logic programs to describe voting algorithms and which generates explicit examples when the algorithm departs from its specification. When we applied our method and system to analyse the vote counting algorithm used for electing the CADE Board of Trustees, we found that it strictly differs from the standard definition of Single Transferable Vote (STV). We therefore argue that “STV” is a misnomer for the CADE algorithm.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Schürmann, Carsten","Beckert, Bernhard","Gore, Rejeev"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381848"],"event":{"acronym":"CADE","end":"2013-06-14","place":"Lake Placid, NY, USA, us","start":"2013-06-09","title":"The 24th International Conference on Automated Deduction","year":"2013"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["CADE Board of Trustees","First order logic","Linear logic programs","Single Transferable Vote STV","Vote counting algorithms"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"analysing vote counting algorithms via logic and its application to the cade election scheme","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-38574-2_9","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381848","identifier":[{"id":"84879962688","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-26478c02-7cf5-49fd-bdc7-ae6fc28388f1"],"keyword":["CADE Board of Trustees","First-order logic","Linear-logic programs","Single Transferable Vote (STV)","Vote counting algorithms"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-AD914B7E710FC34098454CEFFB0BE346"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-38574-2_9","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics","The Department, Theoretical Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten","key":"schürmannpau","last":"Schürmann","locid":"1313519f-2074-41d6-8b79-589648e37211","name":"Schürmann, Carsten","orcid":"0000-0003-4793-0099","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Bernhard","key":"beckertpau","last":"Beckert","name":"Beckert, Bernhard","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Rejeev","key":"gorepau","last":"Gore","name":"Gore, Rejeev","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-642-38574-2_9","eisbn":["9783642385742"],"isbn":["9783642385735"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"135-144","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"Proceedings of the 16th International Conference on Automated Deduction (CADE-24)","title":"Automated Deduction – CADE-24"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84879962688"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-26478c02-7cf5-49fd-bdc7-ae6fc28388f1"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Analysing Vote Counting Algorithms